  "worked_solution": "A point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k=x\\,i+y\\,j+({x}^{3}-xy)\\,k.\n$$\n\nNow, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain the vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=u\\,i+v\\,j+({u}^{3}-uv)\\,k\n$$",
